# size 80x24
# A real editor drawing a real screen: alt screen, a scrolling region, tildes down the left for
# the rows past the end of the buffer, and a status line vim believes it owns.
#
# Captured with `script -qec "stty rows 24 cols 80; vim -u NONE -N -c 'syntax off' file"`, killed
# rather than quit - a clean quit ends with vim tearing the alt screen down, which would leave
# almost nothing to compare.
# include vim.raw
